DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The kklldduunnllooaadd utility unloads a file which was previously loaded with
     kldload(8).

     The following options are available:

     --ff       Force the unload.  This ignores error returns to MOD_QUIESCE
              from the module and implies that the module should be unloaded
              even if it is currently in use.  The users are left to cope as
              best they can.

     --vv       Be more verbose.

     --ii _i_d    Unload the file with this ID.

     --nn _n_a_m_e  Unload the file with this name.

     _n_a_m_e     Unload the file with this name.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The kklldduunnllooaadd utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     kldunload(2), kldload(8), kldstat(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
